rejected the plan as inadequate.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Russia strikes Zelenskyy's hometown, killing 2</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:30bf6f094117acc05f01cfbbb03e9ae2907a978fcca4f4c4cf7f825cd734ebcb</id><updated>2026-11-21T16:15:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T14:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-strikes-zelenskyy-s-hometown-killing-2/a-80009458--1c5b88d83c35.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-strikes-zelenskyy-s-hometown-killing-2/a-80009458?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The attacks follow Russian President Vladimir Putin's vow of a "painful" response to Ukraine's attacks this week on the Kerch Bridge, linking Russian-occupied Crimea.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Anthropic researcher uses AI to solve math's greatest riddle</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:496cc1118362e98e80bb615485fee59660b9625e6a5c1f25180c733274b24351</id><updated>2026-11-21T16:15:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T10:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/anthropic-researcher-uses-ai-to-solve-math-s-greatest-riddle/a-80008428--770513448c0a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/anthropic-researcher-uses-ai-to-solve-math-s-greatest-riddle/a-80008428?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The proposed breakthrough could reshape mathematical research, but still needs independent verification. It's the latest in a string of cases where AI has outpaced humans in solving famous maths problems.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Man convicted of arson over deadly 2025 Palisades fire in Los Angeles</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5be0bb01636f728cd0610d0d0ca1dbbb27c561ab5312f0c10978e1a0f6fb390b</id><updated>2026-11-21T16:14:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T07:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/man-convicted-of-arson-over-deadly-2025-palisades-fire-in-los-angeles/a-80007933--9f183d2c9cc1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/man-convicted-of-arson-over-deadly-2025-palisades-fire-in-los-angeles/a-80007933?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A 30-year-old man has been convicted of causing one of the most destructive wildfires in the history of Los Angeles. The verdict came after the case was retried.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil ex-President Jair Bolsonaro taken to hospital over abdominal pain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0d8e6616ecfe4c6cbf117f4826f9d563acc652e946c65ccc89181ed36d5ff5a1</id><updated>2026-11-21T16:14:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T03:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/brazil-ex-president-jair-bolsonaro-taken-to-hospital-over-abdominal-pain/a-80007648--e735cc923d74.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/brazil-ex-president-jair-bolsonaro-taken-to-hospital-over-abdominal-pain/a-80007648?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Jair Bolsonaro has been hospitalized in Brasilia with intestinal obstruction. The former far-right Brazilian leader is receiving pain medications, his son Carlos said.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russian ornithologist jailed over small donations to Navalny's foundation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5f0ecf869643130d77bd6916501223c9a9bf9865a599577ba98a1541c7796e7e</id><updated>2026-11-21T16:14:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T20:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russian-ornithologist-jailed-over-small-donations-to-navalny-s-foundation/a-80005505--49dba4e1f94e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russian-ornithologist-jailed-over-small-donations-to-navalny-s-foundation/a-80005505?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Sofia Rosenfeld has devoted her life to studying Arctic birds. A Russian court sentenced her to 3.5 years in a penal colony over donations to Navalny's foundation. Friends and family are fighting for her release.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Repression against Iranian lawyers increases</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d16f0d68132097d8b5891bed0bfe0af563be74c075bb3a9c08e9180dcbdaa901</id><updated>2026-11-21T16:14:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T20:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/repression-against-iranian-lawyers-increases/a-80006742--c2e9244e707c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/repression-against-iranian-lawyers-increases/a-80006742?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At least 135 lawyers in Iran have been subjected to repressive measures over the past year. UN experts warn that this seriously jeopardizes the right of those accused to trial in a constitutional court.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Is Pakistan backing anti-Taliban groups in Afghanistan?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:effff15f11532eed9bcd2d881c3b0b434df708c96e3604e7618cc3ba7465e4f0</id><updated>2026-11-21T16:14:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T15:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-pakistan-backing-anti-taliban-groups-in-afghanistan/a-80004814--1a7b1c3175b8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-pakistan-backing-anti-taliban-groups-in-afghanistan/a-80004814?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Taliban rulers in Afghanistan have accused Pakistan of aiding and sheltering armed resistance groups. The allegations come amid heightened tensions and are likely to deepen the rift between the two neighbors.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>EU and UK strike 'landmark deal' to strengthen ties after Brexit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:19190f3535698f8673e9a2ed68db0ccce0722295d6bffabe21852613a46ee2c7</id><updated>2026-11-21T16:14:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T14:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-and-uk-strike-landmark-deal-to-strengthen-ties-after-brexit/a-80001076--f12586fcea84.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-and-uk-strike-landmark-deal-to-strengthen-ties-after-brexit/a-80001076?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Union and the United Kingdom have agreed on "landmark" deals on youth mobility and trade. Leaders on both sides praised the agreement as they seek to rebuild ties.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey takes control of opposition broadcaster Sozcu TV</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:613c0cc0c110c7aab062a8afe3e746009d47597fde68eea94c22879f5065dc90</id><updated>2026-11-21T16:14:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T14:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/turkey-takes-control-of-opposition-broadcaster-sozcu-tv/a-80001984--d9f6e0119d22.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/turkey-takes-control-of-opposition-broadcaster-sozcu-tv/a-80001984?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In the latest in a series of raids and arrests, another major pro-opposition Turkish broadcaster has been brought under state control. This is the third in a year.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Africa at COP31: Will climate cash finally flow?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bbf018adb3fe081658dd14fa1854d1a7fa1abfadf5fae3e3ebe604531ebd2225</id><updated>2026-11-21T16:14:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T14:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/africa-at-cop31-will-climate-cash-finally-flow/a-80002269--5d2b279256b3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/africa-at-cop31-will-climate-cash-finally-flow/a-80002269?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As the curtains draw to a close on COP31 in Antalya, one question looms large for African countries: Will climate promises finally translate into the funding African communities need to cope with a warming world?</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
